:solution
$()	
!if $val55=~1 or $val55=~2 
$()	<p>Avec le ratio 
!insmath $val46
$(), le partage est composé de 
!insmath $val26 \plus $val27 \plus $val28 = $val30
$() parts égales.</p>	<p>Chaque part est composée de 
!insmath \frac{$val31}{$val30}=$val32
$() $(val37[$val44]).</p>	<p>$val21 reçoit 
!insmath $val26 \times $val32=$val33
$() $(val37[$val44]).</p>	<p>$val22 reçoit 
!insmath $val27 \times $val32=$val34
$() $(val37[$val44]).</p>	<p>$val23 reçoit 
!insmath  $val28 \times $val32=$val35
$() $(val37[$val44]).</p> 
!endif
$()	
!if $val55=~3 
$()<br>Avec le ratio 
!insmath $val46
$(), $val21 reçoit $val26 $val39, $val22 reçoit $val27 $val41 et $val23 reçoit $val28 $val43.	<br>Par conséquent, le partage est composé de $val30 parts égales.<br />	$val21 reçoit alors 
!insmath \frac{$val26}{$val30}
$() des $val31 $(val37[$val44]).<br />	C'est à dire 
!insmath \frac{$val26}{$val30} \times $val31 = $val33
$() $(val37[$val44]).<br />	De même, $val22 reçoit 
!insmath \frac{$val27}{$val30}
$() des $val31 $(val37[$val44]).<br />	C'est à dire 
!insmath \frac{$val27}{$val30} \times $val31=$val34
$() $(val37[$val44]).<br />	Et $val23 reçoit 
!insmath \frac{$val28}{$val30} 
$() des $val31 $(val37[$val44]).<br />	<C'est à dire, 
!insmath \frac{$val28}{$val30} \times $val31=$val35
$() $(val37[$val44]).<br />	Ainsi, $val21 reçoit $val33 $(val37[$val44]), $val22 reçoit $val34 $(val37[$val44])	et $val23 reçoit $val35 $(val37[$val44]).<br /> 
!endif
$()	
!if $val55=~4 
$()"<b>$val21</b>,<b>$val22</b>,<b>$val23</b> se partagent <b>
!insmath $val31
$()</b> $(val37[$val44]) selon le ratio <b>
!insmath  $val46 
$()</b>" signifie que lorsque $val21 reçoit <b>
!insmath  $val26
$()</b> $(val38[$val44]) alors	$val22 reçoit <b>
!insmath  $val27
$()</b> $(val40[$val44]) et $val23 reçoit<b>
!insmath  $val28
$()</b> $(val42[$val44]) , ce qui permet de remplir la 1ère ligne du tableau.	<table class="wimscenter wimsborder">	<tr>	<td colspan="1">$val21</td>	<td colspan="1">$val22</td>	<td colspan="1">$val23</td>	<td colspan="1">Total</td>	</tr>	<tr>	<td colspan="1">$(val36[1])</td>	<td colspan="1">$(val36[2])</td>	<td colspan="1">$(val36[3])</td>	<td colspan="1">$val30</td>	</tr>	<tr>	<td colspan="1"></td>	<td colspan="1"></td>	<td colspan="1"></td>	<td colspan="1">$val31</td>	</tr>	</table>	Le ratio traduisant une situation de proportionnalité, on détermine le coefficient de proportionnalité&nbsp;: 
!insmath \frac{$val31}{$val30}=$val32
$().	<p>
!insmath  $val26 \times $val32 = $val33
$() ,
!insmath  $val27 \times $val32 = $val34
$() et 
!insmath  $val28 \times $val32 = $val35
$() .</p> <p>Cela permet de remplir la 2nde ligne du tableau et de conclure .<p>	<table class="wimscenter wimsborder">	<tr>	<td colspan="1">$val21</td>	<td colspan="1">$val22</td>	<td colspan="1">$val23</td>	<td colspan="1">Total</td>	</tr>	<tr>	<td colspan="1">$(val36[1])</td>	<td colspan="1">$(val36[2])</td>	<td colspan="1">$(val36[3])</td>	<td colspan="1">$val30</td>	</tr>	<tr>	<td colspan="1">$val33</td>	<td colspan="1">$val34</td>	<td colspan="1">$val35</td>	<td colspan="1">$val31</td>	</tr>	</table>	<ul class="wims_nopuce" style="padding-left:0px">	  <li>$val21 recevra $val33 $(val37[$val44]),</li>	  <li>$val22 recevra $val34 $(val37[$val44]),</li>	  <li>$val23 recevra $val35 $(val37[$val44]).</li>	</ul> 
!endif
$()	
$()
!exit

